Feign Death	KEY:Rogue ACF ~ Feign Death (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RogueACF.RogueEvasion	PRECLASS:1,Rogue=2	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Rogue Feign Death (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:Alternative class feature (rogue, 2nd level). As an immediate action you enter a catatonic state indistinguishable from death: you cannot see or feel, but still smell, hear and follow what goes on; you are immune to mind-affecting spells and abilities, poison, sleep, paralysis, stunning, disease, ability drain, negative levels and death effects; raise dead or reincarnation fail (resurrection and true resurrection end it); status and deathwatch show you dead; a Heal check (DC 15 + half your level + Constitution modifier) reveals you alive. You can remain so indefinitely (still needing food, water and air); emerging is a standard action. Replaces evasion.
Feign Death	KEY:ACF ~ Rogue Feign Death (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Rogue Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.482	DESC:As an immediate action you enter a catatonic state indistinguishable from death: you cannot see or feel, but still smell, hear and follow what goes on; you are immune to mind-affecting spells and abilities, poison, sleep, paralysis, stunning, disease, ability drain, negative levels and death effects; raise dead or reincarnation fail (resurrection and true resurrection end it); status and deathwatch show you dead; a Heal check (DC 15 + half your level + Constitution modifier) reveals you alive. You can remain so indefinitely (still needing food, water and air); emerging is a standard action. Replaces evasion.

###Block: Ranger alternative class features
Golarion Ranger	KEY:Ranger ACF ~ Golarion Ranger (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RangerACF.RangerWildEmpathy	PRECLASS:1,Ranger=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Golarion Ranger (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.484	DESC:Alternative class feature (ranger, 1st level). Rangers of a military unit who focus on a single animal: upon gaining an animal companion at 4th level he chooses a single type of animal from the basic list available at 4th level and can never call a different companion; his effective druid level for it is his ranger level - 2 (%1) instead of half his level (applied). Replaces wild empathy.
Golarion Ranger	KEY:ACF ~ Golarion Ranger (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Ranger Class Feature	BONUS:VAR|AnimalCompanionLVL|(RangerLVL-2)-floor(RangerLVL/2)|PREVARGTEQ:RangerLVL,4	SOURCEPAGE:p.484	DESC:Rangers of a military unit who focus on a single animal: upon gaining an animal companion at 4th level he chooses a single type of animal from the basic list available at 4th level and can never call a different companion; his effective druid level for it is his ranger level - 2 (%1) instead of half his level (applied). Replaces wild empathy.|RangerLVL-2
Natural Born Ranger	KEY:Ranger ACF ~ Natural Born Ranger (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RangerACF.RangerNaturalBorn	PRECLASS:1,Ranger=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Natural Born Ranger (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.487	DESC:Alternative class feature (ranger, 1st level). Alternative racial traits for characters who begin play as 1st-level rangers, scorning their culture's lessons for what they teach themselves (choose your race's in the category below; the DM should understand them well before allowing them).
Natural Born Ranger	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Ranger (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Ranger Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Ranger ACF Natural Born Ranger|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.487	DESC:Alternative racial traits for characters who begin play as 1st-level rangers, scorning their culture's lessons for what they teach themselves (choose your race's in the category below; the DM should understand them well before allowing them).
Natural Born Ranger (Dwarf)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Ranger (DMC) ~ Dwarf	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFNaturalBornRanger.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Dwarf%	SOURCEPAGE:p.487	DESC:The dwarf ranger loses stonecunning, the racial bonuses on Appraise and Craft checks and the dodge bonus to AC against giants (remove by hand); he gains a dodge bonus to AC against his favored enemies equal to half his favored enemy bonus against them.
Natural Born Ranger (Elf)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Ranger (DMC) ~ Elf	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFNaturalBornRanger.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Elf%	SOURCEPAGE:p.487	DESC:Affinity for the terrain of his homeland (choose aquatic, desert, forest, hills, marsh, mountain or plains): +1 on attack and damage rolls in that terrain; outside it, -1 on Wisdom- and Intelligence-based skill checks.
Natural Born Ranger (Gnome)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Ranger (DMC) ~ Gnome	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFNaturalBornRanger.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Gnome%	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=1|CASTERLEVEL=1|Create Water,Detect Poison,Purify Food and Drink	SOURCEPAGE:p.487	DESC:The gnome ranger keeps speak with animals but loses her other spell-like abilities (dancing lights, ghost sound, prestidigitation - remove by hand), casting create water, detect poison and purify food and drink once per day instead (caster level 1st; save DC 10 + Charisma modifier + spell level).
Natural Born Ranger (Half-Elf)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Ranger (DMC) ~ Half-Elf	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFNaturalBornRanger.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Half-Elf%	BONUS:SKILL|Diplomacy,Gather Information|-2	BONUS:SKILL|Handle Animal,Hide|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.487	DESC:The half-elf ranger loses the +2 bonus on Diplomacy and Gather Information checks and gains +2 on Handle Animal and Hide checks instead (applied).
Natural Born Ranger (Half-Orc)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Ranger (DMC) ~ Half-Orc	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFNaturalBornRanger.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Half-Orc%	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Favored Enemy|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.487	DESC:An additional favored enemy at 1st level: humanoid (human) or humanoid (orc) - not the same as his first one - with the normal +2 bonuses, increased like any other favored enemy; but a penalty equal to that favored enemy bonus on all Charisma checks and Charisma-based skills when dealing with members of the despised race (by hand).
Natural Born Ranger (Halfling)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Ranger (DMC) ~ Halfling	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:RangerACFNaturalBornRanger.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Halfling%	BONUS:VAR|HalflingSaveBonus|-1	SOURCEPAGE:p.487	DESC:The halfling ranger loses the +1 luck bonus on all saving throws (applied); she gains a bonus on saving throws and opposed skill checks against her favored enemies equal to half her favored enemy bonus against them.
Solitary Hunting	KEY:Ranger ACF ~ Solitary Hunting (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RangerACF.RangerAnimalCompanion	PRECLASS:1,Ranger=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Solitary Hunting (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.494	DESC:Alternative class feature (ranger, 1st level). A ranger who loses his faith also loses his animal companion (one he already has abandons him at once), becoming even more self-reliant: his favored enemy bonus also applies to his attack rolls against those enemies. Replaces the animal companion.
Solitary Hunting	KEY:ACF ~ Solitary Hunting (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Ranger Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.494	DESC:A ranger who loses his faith also loses his animal companion (one he already has abandons him at once), becoming even more self-reliant: his favored enemy bonus also applies to his attack rolls against those enemies. Replaces the animal companion.
Wasteland Ranger	KEY:Ranger ACF ~ Wasteland Ranger (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RangerACF.RangerEndurance.RangerWoodlandStride	PRECLASS:1,Ranger=3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Wasteland Ranger (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.498	DESC:Alternative class feature (ranger, 3rd level). Rangers of the waste (Sandstorm's variant): Heat Endurance as a bonus feat at 3rd level instead of Endurance (Improved Heat Endurance if he already has it, without its prerequisites); Sandskimmer as a bonus feat at 7th level instead of woodland stride - both Sandstorm feats, not in the repository's Sandstorm data, so add them by hand. Waste Hunter (Ex), 10th level: he chooses a kind of waste-native creature among his favored enemy types (e.g. dunewinders for magical beasts) and gains +2 on weapon damage and on Bluff, Listen, Sense Motive, Spot and Survival checks against it, +2 on saves against its special abilities and DR 2/- against its physical attacks; this replaces the favored enemy gained at 10th level (applied), though his bonuses against earlier favored enemies still increase as normal. Replaces Endurance and woodland stride.
Wasteland Ranger	KEY:ACF ~ Wasteland Ranger (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Ranger Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Favored Enemy|-1|PREVARGTEQ:RangerLVL,10	SOURCEPAGE:p.498	DESC:Rangers of the waste (Sandstorm's variant): Heat Endurance as a bonus feat at 3rd level instead of Endurance (Improved Heat Endurance if he already has it, without its prerequisites); Sandskimmer as a bonus feat at 7th level instead of woodland stride - both Sandstorm feats, not in the repository's Sandstorm data, so add them by hand. Waste Hunter (Ex), 10th level: he chooses a kind of waste-native creature among his favored enemy types (e.g. dunewinders for magical beasts) and gains +2 on weapon damage and on Bluff, Listen, Sense Motive, Spot and Survival checks against it, +2 on saves against its special abilities and DR 2/- against its physical attacks; this replaces the favored enemy gained at 10th level (applied), though his bonuses against earlier favored enemies still increase as normal. Replaces Endurance and woodland stride.
Animal Companions	KEY:Ranger ACF ~ Animal Companions (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.RangerACF.RangerCompanionList	PRECLASS:1,Ranger=4	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Ranger Animal Companions (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.216	DESC:Alternative class feature (ranger, 4th level). The compendium's compilation of all animals eligible as animal companions (p.216) applies to rangers too, by effective druid level (half the ranger's level); the list and its adjustments are described in the druid's Animal Companions entry. (Offered here: the creatures in the core data; it replaces nothing.)
Animal Companions	KEY:ACF ~ Ranger Animal Companions (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Ranger Class Feature	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Badger,Companion ~ Bat,Companion ~ Camel,Companion ~ Dog,Companion ~ Dog (Riding),Donkey,Companion ~ Eagle,Companion ~ Hawk,Companion ~ Horse (Light),Companion ~ Horse (Heavy),Hyena,Companion ~ Owl,Companion ~ Pony,Companion ~ Porpoise,Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Rat),Companion ~ Raven,Companion ~ Shark (Medium),Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Tiny),Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Small),Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Medium),Companion ~ Squid,Companion ~ Wolf	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Ape,Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Badger),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Bat),Companion ~ Bear (Black),Companion ~ Bison,Companion ~ Boar,Companion ~ Cheetah,Companion ~ Leopard,Companion ~ Lizard (Monitor),Companion ~ Shark (Large),Companion ~ Snake (Constrictor),Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Large),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Weasel),Companion ~ Wolverine|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-3	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Ape),Companion ~ Bear (Brown),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Boar),Companion ~ Crocodile (Giant),Companion ~ Dinosaur (Deinonychus),Companion ~ Dinosaur (Elasmosaurus),Companion ~ Lion,Companion ~ Rhinoceros,Companion ~ Snake (Viper/Huge),Companion ~ Tiger,Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Wolf),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Wolverine)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-6	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Bear (Polar),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Lion),Companion ~ Dinosaur (Megaraptor),Companion ~ Shark (Huge),Companion ~ Snake (Constrictor/Giant),Companion ~ Whale (Orca)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-9	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Bear),Companion ~ Elephant,Companion ~ Octopus (Giant)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-12	COMPANIONLIST:Animal Companion|Roc,Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Shark),Companion ~ Squid (Giant),Companion ~ Dire Animal (Dire Tiger),Companion ~ Dinosaur (Triceratops),Companion ~ Dinosaur (Tyrannosaurus)|FOLLOWERADJUSTMENT:-15	SOURCEPAGE:p.216	DESC:The compendium's compilation of all animals eligible as animal companions (p.216) applies to rangers too, by effective druid level (half the ranger's level); the list and its adjustments are described in the druid's Animal Companions entry. (Offered here: the creatures in the core data; it replaces nothing.)

###Block: Barbarian alternative class features
Aquatic Barbarian	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Aquatic Barbarian (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianFastMovement	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=1	PREMOVE:1,Swim=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Aquatic Barbarian (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.96	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 1st level). Barbarians of the waters and shores, adept swimmers: a barbarian with a racial swim speed applies his fast movement bonus (+10 feet) to his swim speed instead of his land speed (applied; only in no, light or medium armor and not with a heavy load), chosen when the feature is gained. Replaces fast movement on land.
Aquatic Barbarian	KEY:ACF ~ Aquatic Barbarian (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	BONUS:MOVEADD|TYPE.Swim|10|!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Heavy	SOURCEPAGE:p.96	DESC:Barbarians of the waters and shores, adept swimmers: a barbarian with a racial swim speed applies his fast movement bonus (+10 feet) to his swim speed instead of his land speed (applied; only in no, light or medium armor and not with a heavy load), chosen when the feature is gained. Replaces fast movement on land.
Berserker Strength	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Berserker Strength (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianRage.BarbarianGreaterRage.BarbarianMightyRage.BarbarianTirelessRage	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Berserker Strength (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.96	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 1st level). Whenever your current hit points are below 5 x your barbarian level (%1), berserker strength activates automatically, any number of times per day: +4 Strength, +2 on saves, damage reduction 2/- (stacking with similar DR) and -2 AC, with a raging barbarian's limits on actions; you cannot end it voluntarily (it ends when you are unconscious, helpless or healed above the threshold). At 11th level (or when you would gain greater rage) +6 Strength, +3 saves, DR 3/-; at 20th (or mighty rage) +8 Strength, +4 saves, DR 4/-. Effects that apply while raging apply while it is active. (Player's Handbook II's repository entry is an unfinished stub.) Replaces rage and its later improvements.
Berserker Strength	KEY:ACF ~ Berserker Strength (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.96	DESC:Whenever your current hit points are below 5 x your barbarian level (%1), berserker strength activates automatically, any number of times per day: +4 Strength, +2 on saves, damage reduction 2/- (stacking with similar DR) and -2 AC, with a raging barbarian's limits on actions; you cannot end it voluntarily (it ends when you are unconscious, helpless or healed above the threshold). At 11th level (or when you would gain greater rage) +6 Strength, +3 saves, DR 3/-; at 20th (or mighty rage) +8 Strength, +4 saves, DR 4/-. Effects that apply while raging apply while it is active. (Player's Handbook II's repository entry is an unfinished stub.) Replaces rage and its later improvements.|5*BarbarianLVL
City Brawler	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ City Brawler (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianProficiencies	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ City Brawler (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.97	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 1st level). The urban slums you grew up in were as dangerous as any wilderness: Improved Unarmed Strike as a bonus feat (applied) and the effects of Two-Weapon Fighting when fighting unarmed, of Improved Two-Weapon Fighting from 6th level and of Greater Two-Weapon Fighting from 11th; only -2 (not -4) when using improvised weapons. Replaces proficiency with martial weapons, medium armor and shields.
City Brawler	KEY:ACF ~ City Brawler (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=ArmorProfLight|TYPE=WeaponProfSimple	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Improved Unarmed Strike	SOURCEPAGE:p.97	DESC:The urban slums you grew up in were as dangerous as any wilderness: Improved Unarmed Strike as a bonus feat (applied) and the effects of Two-Weapon Fighting when fighting unarmed, of Improved Two-Weapon Fighting from 6th level and of Greater Two-Weapon Fighting from 11th; only -2 (not -4) when using improvised weapons. Replaces proficiency with martial weapons, medium armor and shields.
Dashing Step	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Dashing Step (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianTrapSense	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Dashing Step (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.97	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 3rd level). You have mastered rushing into combat: no -2 AC penalty when charging, and a bonus of +%1 (one-third of your barbarian level) to AC against attacks of opportunity when charging. Replaces trap sense.
Dashing Step	KEY:ACF ~ Dashing Step (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.97	DESC:You have mastered rushing into combat: no -2 AC penalty when charging, and a bonus of +%1 (one-third of your barbarian level) to AC against attacks of opportunity when charging. Replaces trap sense.|floor(BarbarianLVL/3)
Devil's Luck	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Devil's Luck (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianDamageReduction	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=7	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Devil's Luck (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.97	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 7th level). You make up for your lack of heartiness with astounding luck: the points of damage reduction you would otherwise have become a luck bonus on all saving throws (+%1 now; applied). Replaces damage reduction.
Devil's Luck	KEY:ACF ~ Devil's Luck (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	BONUS:SAVE|Fortitude,Reflex,Will|floor((BarbarianLVL-4)/3)|TYPE=Luck	SOURCEPAGE:p.97	DESC:You make up for your lack of heartiness with astounding luck: the points of damage reduction you would otherwise have become a luck bonus on all saving throws (+%1 now; applied). Replaces damage reduction.|floor((BarbarianLVL-4)/3)
Fearsome Gaze	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Fearsome Gaze (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianIndomitableWill	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=6	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Fearsome Gaze (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.99	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 6th level). Your merest glance can break a will to fight: +4 on Intimidate checks, using Strength instead of Charisma as the key ability if better (both applied); you and the target must be within 60 feet and see one another. Replaces indomitable will, and your trap sense bonus is reduced by 1 (applied).
Fearsome Gaze	KEY:ACF ~ Fearsome Gaze (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	BONUS:SKILL|Intimidate|4	BONUS:SKILL|Intimidate|max(0,STR-CHA)	BONUS:VAR|TrapSenseBonus|-1	SOURCEPAGE:p.99	DESC:Your merest glance can break a will to fight: +4 on Intimidate checks, using Strength instead of Charisma as the key ability if better (both applied); you and the target must be within 60 feet and see one another. Replaces indomitable will, and your trap sense bonus is reduced by 1 (applied).
Frostfell Barbarian	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Frostfell Barbarian (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianFrostfell	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Frostfell Barbarian (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.100	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 3rd level). Barbarians at home in the frostfell (often riding dire wolves, megaloceroses, tlalusks or woolly mammoths): their trap sense bonus applies on Reflex saves against natural hazards of the frostfell (avalanches, snow-filled crevasses, other frostfell terrain) and to AC against attacks by such hazards, instead of against traps. Replaces the benefits of trap sense (the bonus itself is unchanged).
Frostfell Barbarian	KEY:ACF ~ Frostfell Barbarian (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.100	DESC:Barbarians at home in the frostfell (often riding dire wolves, megaloceroses, tlalusks or woolly mammoths): their trap sense bonus applies on Reflex saves against natural hazards of the frostfell (avalanches, snow-filled crevasses, other frostfell terrain) and to AC against attacks by such hazards, instead of against traps. Replaces the benefits of trap sense (the bonus itself is unchanged).
Golarion Barbarian	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Golarion Barbarian (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianTrapSense	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Golarion Barbarian (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.100	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 3rd level). Barbarians of cold climates (the Lands of the Linnorm Kings, the Realm of the Mammoth Lords, the Worldwound): cold resistance %1 (2 at 3rd level, +2 every three levels, 12 at 18th; applied). Replaces trap sense.
Golarion Barbarian	KEY:ACF ~ Golarion Barbarian (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	BONUS:VAR|ColdResistanceBonus|2*floor(BarbarianLVL/3)	SOURCEPAGE:p.100	DESC:Barbarians of cold climates (the Lands of the Linnorm Kings, the Realm of the Mammoth Lords, the Worldwound): cold resistance %1 (2 at 3rd level, +2 every three levels, 12 at 18th; applied). Replaces trap sense.|2*floor(BarbarianLVL/3)
Hunter	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Hunter (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianRage.BarbarianGreaterRage.BarbarianIndomitableWill.BarbarianTirelessRage.BarbarianMightyRage	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Hunter (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 1st level). A barbarian who prefers crafty hunting over pure ferocity (swap): favored enemy as the ranger, by barbarian level (1st, 5th, 10th ...), and the ranger's archery combat style with improved archery combat style and archery combat style mastery at 2nd, 6th and 11th (Rapid Shot, Manyshot, Improved Precise Shot - only in light or no armor). Replaces rage, greater rage, indomitable will, tireless rage and mighty rage.
Hunter	KEY:ACF ~ Hunter (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	ABILITY:Ranger Class Feature|AUTOMATIC|Ranger ~ Favored Enemy	BONUS:VAR|RangerFavoredEnemyLVL|BarbarianLVL	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Combat Style ~ Archery	DEFINE:RangerCombatTreeTier|0	BONUS:VAR|RangerCombatTreeTier|1|PREVARGTEQ:BarbarianLVL,2	BONUS:VAR|RangerCombatTreeTier|1|PREVARGTEQ:BarbarianLVL,6	BONUS:VAR|RangerCombatTreeTier|1|PREVARGTEQ:BarbarianLVL,11	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:A barbarian who prefers crafty hunting over pure ferocity (swap): favored enemy as the ranger, by barbarian level (1st, 5th, 10th ...), and the ranger's archery combat style with improved archery combat style and archery combat style mastery at 2nd, 6th and 11th (Rapid Shot, Manyshot, Improved Precise Shot - only in light or no armor). Replaces rage, greater rage, indomitable will, tireless rage and mighty rage.
Natural Born Barbarian	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Natural Born Barbarian (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianNaturalBorn	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Natural Born Barbarian (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 1st level). Alternative racial traits for characters who begin play as 1st-level barbarians (choose your race's in the category below; the DM should understand them well before allowing them).
Natural Born Barbarian	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Barbarian (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Barbarian ACF Natural Born Barbarian|1	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:Alternative racial traits for characters who begin play as 1st-level barbarians (choose your race's in the category below; the DM should understand them well before allowing them).
Natural Born Barbarian (Dwarf)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Barbarian (DMC) ~ Dwarf	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:BarbarianACFNaturalBornBarbarian.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Dwarf%	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:The dwarf barbarian loses stonecunning, the racial bonuses on Appraise and Craft checks and the +1 on attack rolls against orcs and goblins (remove by hand); he gains +1 on attack and damage rolls against aberrations and undead while raging.
Natural Born Barbarian (Elf)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Barbarian (DMC) ~ Elf	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:BarbarianACFNaturalBornBarbarian.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Elf%	BONUS:COMBAT|INITIATIVE|-2	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:The elf barbarian can use Rapid Shot while raging even without its prerequisites, but takes a -2 penalty on initiative checks (applied).
Natural Born Barbarian (Gnome)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Barbarian (DMC) ~ Gnome	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:BarbarianACFNaturalBornBarbarian.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Gnome%	SPELLS:Innate|TIMES=1|CASTERLEVEL=1|Cure Minor Wounds,Guidance,Jump,Resistance	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:The gnome barbarian loses speak with animals and the other gnome spell-like abilities (remove by hand), casting cure minor wounds, guidance, jump and resistance (self only) once each per day instead (caster level 1st; save DC 10 + Charisma modifier + spell level).
Natural Born Barbarian (Half-Elf)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Barbarian (DMC) ~ Half-Elf	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:BarbarianACFNaturalBornBarbarian.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Half-Elf%	BONUS:SKILL|Diplomacy,Gather Information|-2	BONUS:SKILL|Intimidate,Survival|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:The half-elf barbarian loses the +2 bonus on Diplomacy and Gather Information checks and gains +2 on Intimidate and Survival checks (applied).
Natural Born Barbarian (Half-Orc)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Barbarian (DMC) ~ Half-Orc	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:BarbarianACFNaturalBornBarbarian.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Half-Orc%	BONUS:SKILL|Intimidate,Survival|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:The half-orc barbarian can never learn to read, even with levels in other classes, nor place ranks in any Knowledge skill (by hand); his contempt for book learning grants +2 on Intimidate and Survival checks (applied).
Natural Born Barbarian (Halfling)	KEY:ACF ~ Natural Born Barbarian (DMC) ~ Halfling	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:BarbarianACFNaturalBornBarbarian.SpecialQuality	PRERACE:1,Halfling%	SOURCEPAGE:p.104	DESC:The halfling barbarian loses the racial bonuses on Climb, Jump and Move Silently checks (remove by hand) and gains a bonus on Hide checks in natural surroundings equal to half her barbarian level (minimum +1).
Relentless Smash	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Relentless Smash (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianMightyRage	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=20	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Relentless Smash (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.107	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 20th level). If you score a critical hit against an opponent or strike him at least three times in the same round, he is stunned for 1d3 rounds; an opponent of your size or smaller must also succeed on a Fortitude save (DC 10 + the total damage you dealt him this round) or be knocked prone. Replaces mighty rage.
Relentless Smash	KEY:ACF ~ Relentless Smash (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.107	DESC:If you score a critical hit against an opponent or strike him at least three times in the same round, he is stunned for 1d3 rounds; an opponent of your size or smaller must also succeed on a Fortitude save (DC 10 + the total damage you dealt him this round) or be knocked prone. Replaces mighty rage.
Unholy Fury	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Unholy Fury (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianFastMovement	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=1	PREALIGN:CE	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Unholy Fury (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.111	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 1st level). Once during a rage, you can unleash your unholy fury to smite a nonchaotic evil creature: add your Charisma bonus to the attack roll and deal +%1 damage (1 per barbarian level); against a chaotic evil creature the smite has no effect but is still used up. Chaotic evil only: with another alignment it reverts to standard rage until your alignment is restored. Replaces fast movement.
Unholy Fury	KEY:ACF ~ Unholy Fury (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.111	DESC:Once during a rage, you can unleash your unholy fury to smite a nonchaotic evil creature: add your Charisma bonus to the attack roll and deal +%1 damage (1 per barbarian level); against a chaotic evil creature the smite has no effect but is still used up. Chaotic evil only: with another alignment it reverts to standard rage until your alignment is restored. Replaces fast movement.|BarbarianLVL
Unshakable	KEY:Barbarian ACF ~ Unshakable (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.BarbarianACF.BarbarianImprovedUncannyDodge	PRECLASS:1,Barbarian=5	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Unshakable (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.111	DESC:Alternative class feature (barbarian, 5th level). You fear nothing: immunity to fear effects (applied). Replaces improved uncanny dodge.
Unshakable	KEY:ACF ~ Unshakable (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Barbarian Class Feature	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Immunity to Fear	SOURCEPAGE:p.111	DESC:You fear nothing: immunity to fear effects (applied). Replaces improved uncanny dodge.

###Block: Improved Domain Powers (p.163)
Improved Power	KEY:Improved Power (DMC)	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	MULT:YES	STACK:YES	CHOOSE:NOCHOICE	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Improved Domain Power|1	PREMULT:1,[PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1],[PRECLASS:1,Paladin=4]	SOURCEPAGE:p.163	DESC:Through long devotion and hours of study you unlock one of the improved granted powers of one of your domains (chosen in the Improved Domain Power category; a paladin uses her deity's domains). You can take this feat multiple times, each time for a new domain; its effects do not stack.
Improved Air Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Air	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Air],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Air],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Air domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Far-Reaching Wind (Su): The touch of your holy symbol imbues a weapon with the essence of air. Air-imbued weapons are guided to their targets by gusts of wind, allowing supernatural accuracy over long distances. While under this effect, ranged weapons have their range increments doubled, and melee weapons may be hurled as thrown weapons with a range increment of 20 feet. Weapons enhanced in this way maintain their increased range for 1 minute. You may use this ability a number of times per day equal to your cleric level.
Improved Animal Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Animal	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Animal],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Animal],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Animal domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Totemic Spirit Companion (Sp): You can call upon the spirits of the natural world to aid you as a full-round action. This functions just like the spell summon nature's ally I using your cleric level as the caster level. All creatures summoned in this way have either the celestial or fiendish template as appropriate to the type of energy you channel. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1). Additional uses of this ability may be expended to summon more powerful creatures, with each additional use spent increasing the spell to the next highest level. For example, a 6th-level cleric could use this ability to cast summon nature's ally I three times per day or summon nature's ally III once per day (or any other combination).
Improved Chaos Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Chaos	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Chaos],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Chaos],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Chaos domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Chaos Curse (Su): A forking beam of multicolored light springs from your outstretched finger and strikes an enemy within 60 feet as a ranged touch attack. If your target fails a Will save (DC 10 + 1/2 your cleric level + your Charisma modifier), it becomes stricken with random misfortune for 1 minute. Each round, the target has a 50%% chance to drop what it is holding (if holding anything) or to provoke an attack of opportunity (if threatened and not holding anything). If neither condition applies, it falls prone. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1).
Improved Death Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Death	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Death],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Death],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Death domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Call of the Grave (Su): Creatures near you feel the inevitability of death and resist attempts to keep them among the living. When activated, all conjuration spells of the healing subschool cast within 30 feet of you heal half as much damage as normal. In addition, spells that restore life, such as raise dead, reincarnate, and resurrection do not function when cast within 30 feet of you. You may use this ability 1 round per day per cleric level you possess. These rounds need not be consecutive.
Improved Destruction Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Destruction	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Destruction],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Destruction],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Destruction domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Shattering Blow (Su): You may, as a free action, infuse your attacks with the destructive force of entropy for 1 round. While under this effect, your natural attacks and all weapons you use in melee are treated as adamantine for the purposes of bypassing damage reduction and object hardness. You may use this ability 1 round per day per cleric level you possess and these rounds need not be consecutive.
Improved Earth Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Earth	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Earth],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Earth],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Earth domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Tremor Step (Su): While standing on a solid, natural surface (caves or fields would both work; the upper floors of a tower would not) you may strike the earth to produce highly localized seismic vibrations. All creatures except you standing on the ground within 20 feet of you must make Balance checks (DC 10 + your cleric level + your Charisma modifier) or fall prone. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1).
Improved Evil Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Evil	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Evil],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Evil],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Evil domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Torture Strike (Su): One living creature touched (requiring a successful melee touch attack) is wracked by agonizing pain, as if a branding iron had struck bare flesh. You gain a bonus on Intimidate checks against an affected creature equal to your cleric level for 1 minute. In addition, the target creature also takes 1d4 points of Strength damage and is nauseated for 1 round. A successful Fortitude save (DC 10 + 1/2 your cleric level + your Charisma modifier) reduces the condition to sickened and negates the Strength damage. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1).
Improved Fire Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Fire	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Fire],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Fire],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Fire domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Flame-Guiding Song (Su): Your voice has a hypnotic power over fire. You can cause flames to lash out at those nearby, attacking one foe within 10 feet of an existing blaze. These hungry flames deal 2d6 points of fire damage and might cause the target to catch fire. The Reflex save DC to avoid catching on fire or to extinguish these flames equals 10 + 1/2 your cleric level + your Charisma modifier. You may also use this ability to automatically extinguish nonmagical fires no larger than a bonfire. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1).
Improved Good Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Good	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Good],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Good],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Good domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Saving Grace (Su): You can grant a divine boon to your allies, assisting them in their endeavors. You can bestow this boon upon an ally within 30 feet as a move action. This boon grants a sacred bonus equal to your Charisma modifier on the next saving throw, attack roll, skill check, or ability check he attempts within the next minute. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1).
Improved Healing Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Healing	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Healing],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Healing],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Healing domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Healing Light (Su): You may channel divine energy as a free action to enhance a spell of the healing subschool. When using this ability, such spells with a range of touch may be cast with a range of close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels). You may use this ability a number of times per day equal to your cleric level.
Improved Knowledge Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Knowledge	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Knowledge],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Knowledge],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Knowledge domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Divine Inspiration (Su): You can glimpse into the mind of your deity, granting you unsurpassed powers of recall and intuition. You can channel divine energy to take to on any Knowledge skill check as if you had ranks in it, even if you are untrained, as a free action. You may add your Charisma bonus to the check in addition to your Intelligence bonus. You may use this ability a number of times per day equal to you cleric level.
Improved Law Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Law	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Law],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Law],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Law domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Zone of Enforced Order (Su): You can emit an aura that makes chaotic creatures uncomfortable. When in effect, all chaotic creatures within 30 feet of you take a -2 penalty on attack rolls, saving throws, skill checks, and ability checks. You may use this ability 1 round per day per cleric level you possess. These rounds need not be consecutive.
Improved Luck Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Luck	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Luck],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Luck],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Luck domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Charmed Existence (Su): You may, as an immediate action, use this ability to gain a +2 luck bonus on an attack roll, saving throw, skill check, or ability check. You must decide to use this ability before you roll and may only use this ability once per round. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1).
Improved Magic Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Magic	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Magic],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Magic],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Magic domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Power Magical Device (Su): You can channel divine energy through a wand, staff, or other charged magical item, powering it with faith rather than the item's own internal reserves. Doing so requires only as much time as is required to activate the item normally (typically a standard action). The magic item produces all its normal effects, but no charge is drained. To power an item, your caster level must be at least equal to the caster level of the item. You cannot use this ability to duplicate spells with an XP or costly material component. Abilities that require multiple charges require you to spend an equal number of uses of this ability. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1).
Improved Protection Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Protection	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Protection],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Protection],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Protection domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Shield of the Martyr (Su): You can prevent harm to others at the cost of your own safety. Whenever an ally within 30 feet takes damage, you can channel divine energy as an immediate action to split the wounds between the target and yourself (each taking half damage; if an odd number you take the extra point of damage). This ability can only be used once per round and only against a single damage source. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1).
Improved Strength Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Strength	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Strength],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Strength],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Strength domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Tremendous Might (Su): You can channel divine power into feats of truly superhuman might. You may add a +6 morale bonus on any Strength-based skill check or Strength check required to break, lift, drag, or push on object. This does not apply to attack or damage rolls, including grapple, sunder, or bull rush attempts. You may use this ability a number of times per day equal to your cleric level.
Improved Sun Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Sun	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Sun],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Sun],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Sun domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Vengeance of Day (Su): Rays of light brighter than the noon sun burst from your raised holy symbol. All within a 30 foot cone must make Will saves (DC 10 + 1/2 your cleric level + your Charisma modifier) or be dazzled for a number of rounds equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum 1 round). Undead and creatures with light blindness or light sensitivity, such as kobolds or drow, are blinded instead on a failed save. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1).
Improved Travel Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Travel	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Travel],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Travel],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Travel domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Second Wind (Su): You touch your holy symbol to a creature, imbuing it with renewed vigor for travel and great speed. You can remove the fatigued condition or make an exhausted creature merely fatigued. If the target creature has neither of these conditions, this ability instead increases the creature's base speed by +30 feet for 1 round. You may use this ability a number of times per day equal to your cleric level.
Improved Trickery Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Trickery	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Trickery],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Trickery],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Trickery domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Miraculous Deception (Su): You can channel divine power to improve the skills you naturally develop in service of your trickster deity. Using this ability grants you a +4 divine bonus on a single Bluff, Disguise, or Hide skill check. You may use this ability a number of times per day equal to your cleric level.
Improved War Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ War	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,War],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,War],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the War domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Piercing Steel Talon (Su): When wielding your deity's chosen weapon, you can channel divine energy into a single deadly blow. You instinctively attack the weakest points of your target's defenses, allowing you to, as a free action, ignore either the target's armor or shield bonus to AC for a single attack. You may use this ability once per day for every two cleric levels you possess (minimum 1), but no more than once per round.
Improved Water Power	KEY:Improved Domain Power ~ Water	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:ImprovedDomainPower.SpecialQuality	PREMULT:1,[PREDOMAIN:1,Water],[PREMULT:2,[PREDEITYDOMAIN:1,Water],[!PRECLASS:1,Cleric=1]]	SOURCEPAGE:p.164	DESC:Improved granted power of the Water domain (activation a standard action without attacks of opportunity unless noted; a paladin uses it as a cleric three levels lower). Waves Protect Their Own (Su): When at least waist deep in water, you can summon a vortex of swift currents and crashing waves to aid your allies and buffet your enemies. Allies within 30 feet suffer no penalties for underwater combat (as if under a freedom of movement effect) and suffer no risk of drowning in even the roughest seas (although if they choose to dive below the waves they can hold their breath no longer than normal). Enemies in the area take a penalty on attack rolls equal to your Charisma modifier due to the impeding flow of the water (having a swim speed does not negate this penalty, although a freedom of movement effect does). You may use this ability 1 round per day per cleric level you possess. These rounds need not be consecutive.
Beast-Wrestling Combat Style	KEY:Combat Style ~ Beast-Wrestling (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.478	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class Feature.Ranger Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RangerCombatStyle	VISIBLE:YES	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Improved Unarmed Strike|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,1],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Improved Grapple|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,2],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Stunning Fist|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,3],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	DESC:Fighting with bare hands and brute strength, originally to capture dangerous animals (such as crocodiles) without harming them. Combat style (2nd): Improved Unarmed Strike; improved combat style (6th): Improved Grapple; combat style mastery (11th): Stunning Fist - only in light or no armor, as the ranger's other combat styles.
Mounted-Combat Combat Style	KEY:Combat Style ~ Mounted-Combat (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.478	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class Feature.Ranger Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RangerCombatStyle	VISIBLE:YES	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Ride-By Attack|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,1],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Spirited Charge|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,2],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Trample|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,3],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	DESC:Using a mount in combat, typically a horse, riding dog or exotic mount as animal companion. Combat style (2nd): Ride-By Attack; improved combat style (6th): Spirited Charge; combat style mastery (11th): Trample - only in light or no armor, as the ranger's other combat styles.
Piscator Combat Style	KEY:Combat Style ~ Piscator (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.478	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class Feature.Ranger Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RangerCombatStyle	VISIBLE:YES	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Exotic Weapon Proficiency(Net)|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,1],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Improved Trip|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,2],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Improved Critical(Trident)|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,3],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	DESC:A net in one hand and a melee weapon (typically a trident) in the other, entangling or tripping foes before striking; Improved Critical is granted for the trident (change the weapon by hand). Combat style (2nd): Exotic Weapon Proficiency (Net); improved combat style (6th): Improved Trip; combat style mastery (11th): Improved Critical (Trident) - only in light or no armor, as the ranger's other combat styles.
Strong-Arm Combat Style	KEY:Combat Style ~ Strong-Arm (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.478	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class Feature.Ranger Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RangerCombatStyle	VISIBLE:YES	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Power Attack|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,1],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Improved Sunder|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,2],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Great Cleave|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,3],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	DESC:Wading into battle wielding the largest weapon she can, relying on strength and the weight of steel. Combat style (2nd): Power Attack; improved combat style (6th): Improved Sunder; combat style mastery (11th): Great Cleave - only in light or no armor, as the ranger's other combat styles.
Throwing Combat Style	KEY:Combat Style ~ Throwing (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.478	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class Feature.Ranger Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RangerCombatStyle	VISIBLE:YES	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Quick Draw|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,1],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Point Blank Shot|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,2],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Far Shot|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,3],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	DESC:Thrown weapons (favored by halflings, some nomadic humans and barbaric humanoids), keeping distance like the archery style. Combat style (2nd): Quick Draw; improved combat style (6th): Point Blank Shot; combat style mastery (11th): Far Shot - only in light or no armor, as the ranger's other combat styles.
Natural Attack Combat Style	KEY:Combat Style ~ Natural Attacks (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.481	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class Feature.Ranger Class Feature.SpecialQuality.RangerCombatStyle	VISIBLE:YES	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Fangshields Ranger ~ Natural Attack Style	ABILITY:FEAT|VIRTUAL|Multiattack|PREMULT:2,[PREVARGTEQ:RangerCombatTreeTier,1],[!PREEQUIP:1,TYPE=Armor.Medium,TYPE=Armor.Heavy]	DESC:Fangshields rangers only: Multiattack at 2nd level (Improved Natural Attack instead with only one kind of natural attack - by hand), Weapon Focus with one natural attack at 6th, and at 11th Weapon Focus with a second natural weapon or Greater Weapon Focus with the only one (by hand), without prerequisites.
